WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.050 --> 00:03.680
[This series contains scenes of violence, self-harm, and potential triggers.]

3
00:02.780 --> 00:05.150
Damn it, I'm late! I'm doomed!

4
00:03.680 --> 00:05.310
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

5
00:05.560 --> 00:08.260
Humanity is waiting for me!

6
00:08.840 --> 00:10.640
Just let humanity keep waiting.

7
00:10.840 --> 00:12.770
I can't. Today's humanity

8
00:12.900 --> 00:14.510
will be giving me money.

9
00:17.590 --> 00:19.160
Ugh, who is it?

10
00:20.290 --> 00:21.620
Hello?

11
00:21.990 --> 00:23.850
It's you, the wicked songwriter.

12
00:24.250 --> 00:25.950
What? The document envelope?

13
00:27.400 --> 00:29.850
Uh-huh. Yes, I have it.

14
00:30.160 --> 00:31.390
Bring it to you?

15
00:31.510 --> 00:32.910
I can't! I'm busy—

16
00:33.160 --> 00:34.460
Damn it.

17
00:37.980 --> 00:39.360
My dear protégé.

18
00:41.160 --> 00:43.930
Get up. This is also part of the training, kiddo.

19
00:44.190 --> 00:45.050
I don't want to!

20
00:45.070 --> 00:46.830
To build your stamina.

21
00:47.090 --> 00:49.150
Put on your shoes and deliver it now!

22
00:49.440 --> 00:50.470
Go quickly.

23
00:51.250 --> 00:51.950
Hurry up!

24
00:52.000 --> 00:52.940
I'm putting on my shoes.

25
00:52.940 --> 00:53.790
Put them on as you go!

26
00:53.790 --> 00:54.790
Get going now.

27
00:55.080 --> 00:56.050
Hurry up!

28
00:56.170 --> 00:57.260
Go!

29
00:57.410 --> 00:58.600
Damn it.

30
01:14.680 --> 01:15.850
Hanyul.

31
01:26.890 --> 01:29.920
I missed you so much, Lee Hanyul.

32
01:34.580 --> 01:37.030
Where on earth have you been hiding?

33
01:37.580 --> 01:39.700
It took me forever to find you.

34
01:45.280 --> 01:47.940
Wake up. Don't play dead.

35
01:48.300 --> 01:49.910
Hey, is he really dead?

36
01:50.039 --> 01:51.380
Murderer.

37
01:53.009 --> 01:55.460
Is this how you talk to a friend, Hanyul?

38
01:56.390 --> 01:59.910
Don't you remember how much I liked you?

39
02:00.860 --> 02:02.380
You liked me too,

40
02:02.560 --> 02:03.840
didn't you?

41
02:04.550 --> 02:05.720
No,

42
02:05.970 --> 02:07.240
I didn't.

43
02:09.000 --> 02:10.160
Hanyul.

44
02:13.150 --> 02:14.680
He said he doesn't like you.

45
02:18.590 --> 02:21.190
You have no business getting involved in this.

46
02:21.540 --> 02:23.560
This is the hallway of my office.

47
02:27.240 --> 02:29.060
This is between Hanyul and me.

48
02:33.060 --> 02:34.840
Then it's half my business too.

49
02:40.579 --> 02:42.720
I'll just pretend you're dead too.

50
02:43.270 --> 02:45.400
Don't ever show up in front of me again.

51
02:57.200 --> 02:59.220
Looks like we're starting over,

52
02:59.320 --> 03:00.440
Hanyul.

53
03:03.310 --> 03:10.140
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

54
03:12.220 --> 03:16.010
[Adapted from the webtoon "The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

55
03:16.020 --> 03:18.760
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

56
03:18.780 --> 03:21.690
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

57
03:38.140 --> 03:39.770
[Yoo Dohyun]

58
03:39.890 --> 03:41.380
[Cho Chanhyeon]

59
03:41.500 --> 03:43.050
[Ko Gyeol]

60
03:44.840 --> 03:48.020
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

61
03:51.270 --> 03:53.070
Didn't you come to bring me that?

62
03:56.920 --> 03:57.860
You know Herod?

63
03:58.040 --> 03:59.390
Why didn't you tell me?

64
03:59.530 --> 04:02.540
It's nothing. He's just an artist under our agency.

65
04:02.550 --> 04:06.310
Wait... Are you two conspiring against me?

66
04:06.810 --> 04:10.340
Couldn't you tell from the atmosphere just now? Obviously not.

67
04:10.450 --> 04:11.630
That aside,

68
04:12.480 --> 04:14.050
were you in love with Herod?

69
04:15.360 --> 04:16.410
He said you used to like him—

70
04:16.410 --> 04:17.630
I wasn't.

71
04:19.019 --> 04:20.310
Right?

72
04:20.560 --> 04:22.050
He's so ugly.

73
04:22.490 --> 04:24.600
He should at least be of my caliber.

74
04:25.510 --> 04:26.650
How much

75
04:26.840 --> 04:28.410
do you know about me?

76
04:28.640 --> 04:30.490
About me and Herod, and...

77
04:30.980 --> 04:32.180
Herod...

78
04:35.000 --> 04:36.730
Want me to get rid of him for you?

79
04:38.290 --> 04:41.480
You look like you're about to bolt over a few words from that bastard.

80
04:41.480 --> 04:42.480
I can't have that.

81
04:42.570 --> 04:43.400
What?

82
04:43.550 --> 04:46.770
I'm not interested in your entanglements with other guys.

83
04:46.770 --> 04:48.440
Focus only on me.

84
04:48.810 --> 04:50.480
Only on me and my songs.

85
04:52.980 --> 04:55.120
I'll do anything for you.

86
04:55.480 --> 04:56.630
Really?

87
04:57.620 --> 04:59.520
What I really want is...

88
05:02.920 --> 05:04.410
Don't follow me.

89
05:17.430 --> 05:18.660
Should I follow him?

90
05:19.210 --> 05:20.490
Don't blow your cover.

91
05:20.770 --> 05:23.230
Make sure he gets home safely, and report back to me.

92
05:23.230 --> 05:24.710
Yes, understood.

93
05:43.170 --> 05:45.210
Thank you, my errand warrior.

94
05:45.340 --> 05:46.700
I'm back.

95
05:46.880 --> 05:48.040
Good job.

96
05:48.070 --> 05:50.070
You're late. Take your punishment.

97
05:50.500 --> 05:51.800
Punishment?

98
05:51.960 --> 05:53.470
Have a big meal.

99
05:55.100 --> 05:56.610
I have no appetite.

100
05:56.780 --> 05:59.150
You don't need an appetite. You eat when it's time.

101
05:59.150 --> 06:01.100
Eat well, and your mind will stop wandering.

102
06:01.100 --> 06:02.570
Go wash your hands now.

103
06:02.970 --> 06:04.170
Yes.

104
06:44.450 --> 06:45.510
Are you going to run away?

105
06:45.510 --> 06:46.710
Are you running away?

106
06:49.480 --> 06:50.690
My dear protégé.

107
06:50.970 --> 06:52.900
The food is getting cold. Hurry up.

108
06:59.100 --> 07:00.610
Here, eat this.

109
07:00.740 --> 07:02.340
Have some of this too.

110
07:03.300 --> 07:05.020
And some dried shredded squid.

111
07:05.020 --> 07:06.800
Eat more anchovies.

112
07:06.810 --> 07:09.120
The calcium is good for your bones. Here.

113
07:16.370 --> 07:18.300
How is it? Is it good?

114
07:21.110 --> 07:23.570
That's right. Okay.

115
07:25.680 --> 07:27.880
[Entertainment Agencies Suspected of Receiving Mob Funds]

116
07:26.730 --> 07:29.760
Allegations have emerged that some prominent entertainment agencies

117
07:29.760 --> 07:32.950
have been operating with funding from organized crime groups.

118
07:32.920 --> 07:36.900
[Entertainment Agencies Suspected of Receiving Mob Funds]

119
07:32.960 --> 07:36.740
The police have launched an investigation after uncovering evidence

120
07:36.740 --> 07:39.770
of the mob's active involvement— exerting pressure

121
07:39.780 --> 07:43.670
regarding artist contracts and investment recoupment.

122
07:46.060 --> 07:49.460
Right, watching the news while eating gives me indigestion.

123
07:50.700 --> 07:53.150
Right. Try the kimchi too.

124
07:54.720 --> 07:56.850
This batch is loaded with probiotics.

125
07:56.909 --> 07:58.170
It was well fermented.

126
07:58.190 --> 07:59.980
-Have a quail egg. -Okay.

127
08:00.140 --> 08:02.490
Here, get it. Good.

128
08:03.670 --> 08:05.330
My rice is completely buried.

129
08:06.110 --> 08:07.390
Eat more.

130
08:07.510 --> 08:10.760
Fuel up. Tomorrow will be an eventful day.

131
08:15.770 --> 08:19.610
[Whistleblower Exposes Alleged Ties Between Entertainment Agency & Criminal Syndicate]

132
08:25.170 --> 08:26.200
Damn it!

133
08:30.170 --> 08:31.420
I'm sorry.

134
08:32.090 --> 08:33.409
Which rat is it?

135
08:33.650 --> 08:34.669
We're looking into it.

136
08:34.669 --> 08:37.090
Looking into it? You should be stopping it, Won!

137
08:37.090 --> 08:39.929
Do you think I sent you there to make music?

138
08:40.080 --> 08:41.210
I'm sorry.

139
08:46.730 --> 08:47.800
Won.

140
08:48.620 --> 08:49.640
Yes.

141
08:50.890 --> 08:52.410
Anything new these days?

142
08:53.470 --> 08:54.440
No.

143
08:55.220 --> 08:58.790
You'd better not be hiding anything from me.

144
09:01.340 --> 09:02.580
We're done here.

145
09:12.780 --> 09:16.270
[Sandol Village]

146
09:13.500 --> 09:16.390
-Here, have the big one. -Okay, okay.

147
09:16.290 --> 09:19.330
[Special Celebratory Performance by a Popular Singer From Seoul]

148
09:16.670 --> 09:17.540
I want one more.

149
09:17.700 --> 09:19.570
One is a bit stingy, don't you think?

150
09:19.570 --> 09:20.630
-Cheers. -Cheers.

151
09:20.720 --> 09:22.570
-Cheers! -Cheers. Cheers.

152
09:23.110 --> 09:25.790
Gosh, Mr. Pan, why are you so late?

153
09:26.240 --> 09:28.650
Mr. Pan, didn't you say we were going for a walk?

154
09:28.650 --> 09:29.580
How did we get here?

155
09:29.580 --> 09:31.630
We walked here, didn't we?

156
09:31.780 --> 09:33.580
This is a disaster!

157
09:33.900 --> 09:36.210
Sandol Village really can't do without me.

158
09:36.210 --> 09:38.030
What's wrong now, Chief?

159
09:38.390 --> 09:40.320
The microphone is screeching,

160
09:40.460 --> 09:42.190
and the singer hasn't shown up.

161
09:42.310 --> 09:43.990
Maybe the mic is heartbroken.

162
09:44.120 --> 09:45.650
Why hasn't the singer arrived?

163
09:45.650 --> 09:47.510
They said they took the wrong way.

164
09:47.580 --> 09:50.710
They went to Sandeul Village instead of Sandol Village.

165
09:51.040 --> 09:52.200
It happens.

166
09:52.270 --> 09:54.280
-This is troublesome. What should we do? -Exactly.

167
09:54.280 --> 09:55.050
Sit first. Sit.

168
09:55.050 --> 09:55.900
Sit down.

169
09:56.140 --> 09:57.130
Take a seat.

170
09:59.850 --> 10:00.680
Alright.

171
10:01.190 --> 10:02.540
Hello.

172
10:05.510 --> 10:06.770
I'm good. Thank you.

173
10:08.540 --> 10:09.830
No, thank you. Really.

174
10:11.960 --> 10:13.030
Just eat it.

175
10:13.140 --> 10:16.870
In Sandol Village, refusing three times is considered rebellion.

176
10:17.640 --> 10:18.910
Thank you.

177
10:25.620 --> 10:26.550
Okay, everyone!

178
10:26.690 --> 10:27.640
Everyone!

179
10:27.970 --> 10:29.570
The singer is here!

180
10:29.650 --> 10:31.090
-The singer? Where? -Where?

181
10:31.090 --> 10:32.030
-Where? -Where?

182
10:32.100 --> 10:32.830
Here!

183
10:33.000 --> 10:33.630
Here?

184
10:33.820 --> 10:35.820
-Me? -Yeah.

185
10:35.950 --> 10:37.680
I didn't say I was going to sing.

186
10:37.700 --> 10:39.690
But you're eating the appearance deposit.

187
10:39.690 --> 10:40.600
Huh?

188
10:42.010 --> 10:43.610
Bravo! Come on!

189
10:44.850 --> 10:46.490
So that's the singer.

190
10:46.620 --> 10:48.160
-Mr. Pan. -Please.

191
10:48.300 --> 10:49.220
Mr. Pan.

192
10:49.630 --> 10:50.940
Please get on stage.

193
10:53.840 --> 10:54.810
Mr. Pan!

194
10:57.940 --> 10:59.480
Attention, everyone.

195
10:59.720 --> 11:03.710
A round of applause for our special guest singer!

196
11:06.970 --> 11:07.990
Hello, everyone.

197
11:08.120 --> 11:10.660
A little introduction: born and raised in Sandol Village—not,

198
11:10.660 --> 11:14.510
but he just ate our specialty, Sandol sweet and sour pork.

199
11:14.640 --> 11:16.420
He ate it yesterday, ate it last year,

200
11:16.420 --> 11:17.660
and just ate it again!

201
11:17.820 --> 11:22.580
This is Lee Hanyul, a superstar shaped by Sandol Village!

202
11:25.440 --> 11:27.130
Music!

203
11:44.180 --> 11:48.110
Dawn always comes softly...

204
11:48.290 --> 11:49.290
I can't hear you!

205
11:51.390 --> 11:53.860
Where is his energy?

206
11:54.100 --> 11:55.830
He looks just like my grandson.

207
11:57.130 --> 11:59.220
You can't make him sing on an empty stomach!

208
11:59.220 --> 12:01.010
They can't hear well!

209
12:01.490 --> 12:02.560
Just this once—

210
12:02.970 --> 12:04.870
if I could...

211
12:05.040 --> 12:11.730
If I could turn back time.

212
12:11.850 --> 12:13.510
The sound of dawn...

213
12:13.710 --> 12:14.510
That's right!

214
12:14.520 --> 12:17.880
My breath calling out to you.

215
12:19.320 --> 12:26.350
It may fade into the distance, yet it still reaches toward you.

216
12:26.620 --> 12:28.910
The sound of dawn...

217
13:39.430 --> 13:40.470
Young man!

218
13:40.640 --> 13:43.040
Where are you from? How can you sing so well?

219
13:43.070 --> 13:44.270
Where are you from?

220
13:44.310 --> 13:45.640
You have such fair skin.

221
13:45.680 --> 13:46.730
And what a voice!

222
13:46.890 --> 13:49.850
Your singing could melt any woman's heart.

223
13:49.990 --> 13:52.070
My heart is a puddle right now!

224
13:53.910 --> 13:55.310
Wait...

225
13:56.320 --> 13:57.560
Thank you.

226
13:57.800 --> 13:59.870
And who is this tall hunk?

227
14:00.600 --> 14:01.950
He is mine.

228
14:02.120 --> 14:04.000
-Oh my! -Oh my, oh my!

229
14:04.240 --> 14:06.250
They must be a couple!

230
14:06.610 --> 14:07.840
It's not like that.

231
14:07.970 --> 14:09.630
I'm a singer under his agency.

232
14:09.980 --> 14:13.450
I had my own season of hot passion, too.

233
14:13.630 --> 14:16.430
What are you talking about? It's still not too late for us.

234
14:16.430 --> 14:17.510
What do you mean?

235
14:17.640 --> 14:19.870
Should I tell my husband to set the mood tonight?

236
14:19.870 --> 14:21.070
How? Set what mood?

237
14:21.190 --> 14:23.320
Get him to do some push-ups to prepare!

238
14:23.460 --> 14:24.650
Like this.

239
14:26.930 --> 14:28.290
Don't follow me.

240
14:29.650 --> 14:30.650
He's so handsome.

241
14:30.810 --> 14:31.520
Oh my god.

242
14:31.670 --> 14:33.070
How can he be so handsome?

243
14:36.240 --> 14:37.970
I just want to go along with him!

244
14:56.750 --> 14:57.900
Hello.

245
14:59.030 --> 14:59.880
Hello.

246
15:00.010 --> 15:01.380
I saw you singing.

247
15:01.420 --> 15:02.680
You have a great voice.

248
15:02.830 --> 15:03.920
Thank you.

249
15:04.060 --> 15:05.530
I was lucky to catch you.

250
15:05.830 --> 15:08.250
I was just passing by on an errand.

251
15:08.490 --> 15:10.150
I forgot to introduce myself.

252
15:10.550 --> 15:11.740
I'm...

253
15:12.340 --> 15:15.520
Go Hyunwoo, head of rookie development at Saebyeok Entertainment.

254
15:13.610 --> 15:15.400
[Saebyeok Entertainment: I like your voice. Reach out anytime!]

255
15:21.530 --> 15:22.840
He is mine.

256
15:24.100 --> 15:24.930
Um,

257
15:25.100 --> 15:26.320
at least take my card.

258
15:26.710 --> 15:28.280
I said he is mine.

259
15:33.740 --> 15:34.770
Cheers.

260
15:52.580 --> 15:53.800
What are you doing?

261
15:53.960 --> 15:55.420
I was getting a tissue.

262
15:55.560 --> 15:56.400
What's wrong?

263
16:23.950 --> 16:25.880
-What? -I'm going to the restroom.

264
16:40.510 --> 16:41.860
Don't follow me.

265
16:48.510 --> 16:49.990
I told you not to follow me!

266
16:53.200 --> 16:54.470
Long time no see.

267
17:05.000 --> 17:07.260
You were in cahoots with that guy, right?

268
17:10.380 --> 17:12.430
That was aggravated assault.

269
17:14.040 --> 17:15.560
Attempted murder.

270
17:16.270 --> 17:17.480
Let go of me.

271
17:19.530 --> 17:21.790
I guess I should get the police involved.

272
17:23.240 --> 17:25.300
I wonder what will happen to that guy.

273
17:32.650 --> 17:34.030
Oh, you're still here?

274
17:35.370 --> 17:36.600
I guessed so.

275
17:37.150 --> 17:39.350
It's better not make a big deal out of it,

276
17:39.620 --> 17:40.650
right?

277
17:45.190 --> 17:47.390
You could compensate me with your body.

278
17:48.600 --> 17:51.000
We have to finish what we started last time.

279
17:56.900 --> 17:58.040
God damn it!

280
17:58.050 --> 17:59.260
Wow, seriously!

281
18:01.110 --> 18:02.090
Bring it on!

282
18:02.490 --> 18:03.640
Lee Won.

283
18:10.000 --> 18:11.540
I'm sorry about last time.

284
18:13.580 --> 18:16.780
I mistook you for a pervert and reacted without thinking.

285
18:18.780 --> 18:20.950
Jeez, there goes my chance to throw hands.

286
18:20.950 --> 18:22.090
Oh, man.

287
18:22.380 --> 18:23.840
Sheesh. Damn it.

288
18:24.740 --> 18:25.670
I knew it.

289
18:25.740 --> 18:27.320
You two really are in cahoots.

290
18:27.320 --> 18:28.580
Bloody hell.

291
18:30.960 --> 18:32.830
Give me your number,

292
18:32.930 --> 18:36.730
and I'll take care of your medical bills and any other compensation.

293
18:37.050 --> 18:38.170
Tsk.

294
18:44.120 --> 18:45.410
Okay.

295
18:46.340 --> 18:48.180
Now you're talking my language.

296
18:52.230 --> 18:53.570
Make way, won't you?

297
18:54.560 --> 18:55.890
I'll go around you then.

298
18:58.600 --> 19:00.070
Right. Almost forgot.

299
19:04.700 --> 19:06.130
Smile.

300
19:09.970 --> 19:11.610
Bye, pretty boy.

301
19:40.010 --> 19:40.820
Lee Won.

302
19:41.010 --> 19:42.130
Hey!

303
19:42.370 --> 19:43.900
Where are you going?

304
19:44.040 --> 19:45.040
Lee Won!

305
19:57.050 --> 19:58.280
I'm so full.

306
20:00.210 --> 20:02.460
-Mr. Pan. -Hmm?

307
20:03.140 --> 20:04.970
I have a question.

308
20:05.620 --> 20:06.620
I like questions.

309
20:06.710 --> 20:07.780
Go ahead.

310
20:09.560 --> 20:11.870
What kind of person is Lee Won?

311
20:16.690 --> 20:18.530
It's not that.

312
20:18.710 --> 20:20.730
Since we're working together,

313
20:20.940 --> 20:23.070
I should probably know more about him.

314
20:24.060 --> 20:25.910
That's a relief.

315
20:26.310 --> 20:27.570
What do you mean?

316
20:28.730 --> 20:34.090
He's too high maintenance— not worth the drama.

317
20:34.710 --> 20:39.130
He must have everything he wants.

318
20:39.300 --> 20:41.380
And the problem is,

319
20:41.740 --> 20:46.850
because of that, he always crosses the line and creates trouble.

320
20:46.860 --> 20:48.090
That's his problem.

321
20:48.670 --> 20:51.680
So don't get too close to him,

322
20:51.940 --> 20:53.160
or you'll get hurt.

323
20:56.530 --> 20:59.110
Well, it might be too late for you now.

324
21:01.290 --> 21:02.290
Damn it.

325
21:06.520 --> 21:08.050
Where are the stars?

326
21:43.790 --> 21:47.590
Why on earth are you doing this?

327
21:51.850 --> 21:53.110
Look carefully.

328
